  * mx.lvl to 193), gpu_smmu=1 (read the GPU SMMU GR0 state at 0x5040000) and
  * gpu_norelease=1, which stops after the preset so the clock and rail
  * changes can be measured with the CM3 still in reset.
+ * log50 never came back to USB: with the CM3 held in reset nothing wedges, so
+ * the machine stayed in iOS instead of dying back to recovery. That is why
+ * 0108 adds gpu_reboot (call reboot_kernel(RB_QUICK) at the end of the probe,
+ * so a surviving boot returns to recovery by itself) and gpu_stub, which
+ * replaces the firmware's entry point with sixteen words of our own Thumb code
+ * and nothing else: every exception vector points at the same loop, so a fault
+ * cannot walk into the half-written image table. Stub 1 spins; stub 2 first
+ * stores 0x5EED1234 to TCM 0x130 and then repeats the image's own init-result
+ * write from offset 0x2eb0 - `str 0xBABEFACE, [0x81714]` - taking both
+ * operands out of the image's own literal pool, so the CM3 address of the
+ * register block never has to be derived. A hang at the release with stub 1 is
+ * the core or its clock, not the firmware's memory traffic; 0xBABEFACE in
+ * FW_INIT_RESULT with stub 2 proves the CM3 runs and its register writes land
+ * where the host reads.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
+#include <sys/reboot.h>
 #include <kern/clock.h>
 #include <machine/machine_routines.h>
